modify uvmcopy(): clear PTE_W, set PTE_COW, map and add the reference count of the page.
modify usertrap(): add copyonwrite() to it.
modify copyout(): add copyonwrite() to it.
modify kalloc(): set reference count to 1.
modify kfree(): decrease reference count and free the memory if equals 0.

<core function>
copyonwrite(): clear PTE_COW, restore PTE_W, allocate physcial memory, unmap the original page and map the new page.

some tips for passing usertests:
1. if mappages() failed, remember to unmap all the pages and free them.
2. check if (va > MAXVA)
3. race condition check: reference count lock?
4. index of reference count array: (pa - KERNBASE) / PGSIZE
5. remember to kill the process if error occurred
6. kfree() is the final step for freeing memory, so put the decreasement work of reference count into it.
